int(equipment_summary)\\n\", \"# Check: one row per equipment; columns named mean and count.\\n\", \"\\n\"], \"execution_count\": null, \"outputs\": []}, {\"cell_type\": \"markdown\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"## Task 7: Reuse your statistics in one function — 5 marks · about 15 minutes\\n\", \"\\n\", \"Turn three calculations from Task 5 into a reusable function. The supplied inputs are a DataFrame (`table`) and a column name (`column_name`).\\n\", \"Return a dictionary with keys `mean`, `sum`, `median`, calculated from `table[column_name]`. Replace the three `None` values. Use the inputs rather than a fixed column or the global `cleaned_data`.\\n\", \"Then call your function for `cleaned_data` and `\\\"target\\\"`, and again for `\\\"load_pct\\\"`. Display both results. The grader tests the function with other numeric values (5 marks).\"]}, {\"cell_type\": \"code\", \"metadata\": {\"tags\": [\"iuea-answer-function\"]}, \"source\": [\"def calculate_column_statistics(table, column_name):  # Do not edit: defines the function inputs used for marking.\\n\", \"    # Repeat Task 5's mean, sum and median calculations on table[column_name].\\n\", \"    # Use these inputs, not the global cleaned_data or a fixed column name.\\n\", \"    # Keep the three quoted keys; replace each None with a calculation.\\n\", \"    return {\\\"mean\\\": None, \\\"sum\\\": None, \\\"median\\\": None}\\n\", \"\\n\", \"# Call the function twice: use cleaned_data with \\\"target\\\", then with \\\"load_pct\\\".\\n\", \"# Pattern: result = function_name(table, \\\"column\\\"); then print(result).\\n\", \"# The target results should match your Task 5 mean, sum and median.\\n\"], \"execution_count\": null, \"outputs\": []}, {\"cell_type\": \"markdown\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"## Task 8: Conditions and a loop — 10 marks · about 20 minutes\\n\", \"\\n\", \"Use a `for` loop over `cleaned_data[\\\"load_pct\\\"]`. Inside it, use `if`, `elif`, `else` to count loads in these categories:\\